ail.asm, ail.inc and ail.mac are the IBM Audio Interface Library (AIL) by John Miles,
Copyright (C) 1991, 1992 Miles Design, Inc. Their headers are kept as written, as text:
they are transcoded from the upstream's CP437 to UTF-8, so their bytes are not the
original's.

This directory is a copy of dqk-disassembly's v11/src/asm/ at 623711e. FRUA and DQK keep
separate source by design. CKIT.EXE's frame 100c is the same 3,253 bytes as DQK.EXE's, at
the same file offset, so the addresses in ail.asm's side comments hold for both.

Origin: John Miles' public AIL2 source release, mirrored at
https://github.com/Tronix286/AIL2 (revision f9c05599bdeb05a0a2b05557f6a23cdafb8550ce),
by way of matrix-disassembly v10/src/ at commit 7e9931f, which returned it to the AIL
2.00 Matrix Cubed links. ail.asm carries five edits that make it the 2.02 that DQK.EXE and
CKIT.EXE link, each with a side comment naming its address, and leaves out matrix's
Pascal P_AIL_* adapters. ail.inc and ail.mac are matrix's, unchanged.

